  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Masarouna: SMEX</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SMEX, a pioneering digital rights organisation in MENA will contribute with lobby and advocacy  efforts  for  legislative  policy  change  at  national  level  as  well  as  international  level, targeting  social  media  companies  such  as  Meta,  Twitter,  TikTok  etc.  in  order  to  make  SRHR content  more  accessible  for  young  people.  The  advocacy  will  be  based  on  raw  data  collected through SMEX&apos;s Digital Safety Helpdesk and online platform Muhal and research on social media companies&#x2019;moderation policies of SRHR content. They will also lead on capacity strengthening on digital security for civil society across the region, which is crucial as the work of CSO&apos;s online comes  under  tighter  state  surveillance.  Finally,  they  will  lead  on  regional  conveningon  digital rights  in  MENA  through  their  annual  Bread  &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt;  Net  conference  which  will  provide  Masarouna partners with an opportunity to share challenges and opportunities at the intersection between digital rights andSRHR. As confirmed by the Masarouna baseline, there is a need to ensure that our work addresses digital rights in order to defend and open up civic space. SMEX, asa Lebanese based  organization  working  regionally,  will  enable  Masarouna  to  defenddigital  rights  from  the SRHR  perspective  and  open  up  the  spaces  for  SRHR  content  to  become  more  accessible  for young people.</narrative>
  </description>
